  "question": {
    "text": "The compound formed as a result of oxidation of ethyl benzene by $\\mathrm{KMnO}_4$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "7A8Sd",
      "text": "\nbenzophenone\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LQ9aM",
      "text": "\nacetophenone\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JDlLN",
      "text": "\nbenzoic acid\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "iphGt",
      "text": "\nbenzyl alcohol",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Any aliphatic carbon with hydrogen attached to it, in combination with benzene ring, will be oxidized to benzoic acid by $\\mathrm{KMnO}_4 / \\mathrm{H}^{+}$.\nHence, (C) is correct.",
    "image": null
  },
